## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge routing with simple feature flag logic using standard nginx capabilities, keeping it beginner-friendly while still requiring practical setup.

## Key Concepts
- nginx upstreams and map for header-driven routing
- TLS termination in docker-compose
- cross-DC networking and service naming

## Code Example
```nginx
http {
  upstream api-old { server api-old:8080; }
  upstream api-new { server api-new:8080; }
  map $http_x_feature_flag_alpha $target { default api-old; 1 api-new; }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    ssl_certificate /certs/server.crt; ssl_certificate_key /certs/server.key;
    location / { proxy_pass http://$target; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test header-driven routing in CI?
- How would you add health checks and a safe rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy correctness across DC failover?
- How would you handle policy module hot-reload and versioning?

## Why This Is Asked

